  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "US air travel slowly recovers from nationwide flight ground stop as chaos continues",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/14/faa-ground-stop-flights-resume-airport-chaos",
      "description": "<p>Thousands of flights still canceled as officials blamed ageing air control system for nationwide grounding</p><p>Travel chaos continued across the US on Saturday morning as airlines worked to recover from Friday’s four-hour nationwide Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/13/faa-ground-stop-flights-explained\">ground stop</a> that delayed or canceled thousands of flights.</p><p>By of 11am ET on Saturday morning, more than 4,000 flights within, into or out of the US had already been canceled, according to <a href=\"https://www.flightaware.com/live/cancelled/\">FlightAware</a>, adding to the more than 8,000 cancellations recorded on Friday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/14/faa-ground-stop-flights-resume-airport-chaos\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T17:11:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "US air travel should recover from ground stop by end of Sunday, FAA says",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/us-air-travel-should-recover-from-ground-stop-by-end-of-sunday-faa-says-126111401330_1.html",
      "description": "US air travel should be fully recovered from the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years by the end of Sunday, FAA Administrator Bryan Bedford said Saturday.\nBedford said the flights \"will still have delays and cancellations\" on Saturday but promised that the \"worst is behind us.\"\nHis comments came as airlines across the US worked to recover from a ground stoppage that lasted four hours, stranding hundreds of thousands of passengers.\nNew technology being added to the nation's air traffic control system overloaded antiquated equipment and caused \"intermittent\" communications and radar gaps, leading to the flight shutdown of more than four hours, Trump administration officials said.\nPlanes were taking flight and landing Saturday, Secretary of Transportation Sean Duffy said. But the effects could be felt for days. Officials say the system will likely return to normal in time to handle the Thanksgiving travel rush.\nThe nationwide stop was the first since January 2023, when another",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-14T16:58:55"
    },
    {
      "title": "Air India says US flights operated as scheduled, with no major delays",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/aviation/air-india-says-us-flights-operated-as-scheduled-with-no-major-delays-126111401234_1.html",
      "description": "Air India on Saturday said all its flights to and from the US operated as scheduled without significant delays, even as thousands of flights were grounded across the country due to communications problems at regional air traffic control centres.\nThe airline also said in a statement that all its flights en route to New York, Newark and San Francisco landed on time early this morning.\nThe statement came after the US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) grounded all flights nationwide Friday afternoon because of communications problems at regional air traffic control centres.\nMore than 2,500 flights were cancelled in the US on Saturday, and hundreds more were delayed, according to FlightAware, a website that tracks flight disruptions.\nThe FAA notice said the ground stop was imposed due to extraordinary circumstances and safety concerns.\n\"All our flights to and from the US have been operating as per schedule without any significant delay in spite of air traffic getting severely impac",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-14T15:25:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "FAA allows flights to resume after hours-long ground stop across the US",
